#DESCRIPTION
Inflow / outflow open-boundary regression test for the HYBRID solver.

A uniform magnetized hybrid plasma streams along +x (sub-Alfvenic, u = 0.2 v_A)
through a 1D domain.  The -x face is an INFLOW boundary (BC::inflow): the ghost
EM field is copied from the adjacent physical cell (zero-gradient) and a drifting
Maxwellian flux is re-seeded in the ghost cells each step, maintaining the
upstream state.  The +x face is an OUTFLOW boundary (BC::outflow): particles
stream out freely and the ghost field is again a zero-gradient copy.

A perfectly uniform streaming plasma is the exact steady solution, so this
validates that the inflow/outflow pair keeps a uniform state uniform: ion
kinetic energy and magnetic energy are conserved, the upstream density and
velocity are preserved at the inflow face, and no spurious electric field
develops.  This is the clean counterpart to the wip/hybrid-bc-regression shock
attempt, which regressed the hybrid solver; here the inflow is built ONLY from
the existing zero-gradient ghost-cell copy (Pic::use_float) and the existing
Maxwellian particle re-seeding (Particles::add_particles_cell), with no extra
flux accumulator or field-relaxation machinery.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
F                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#FIELDBOXBOUNDARY
inflow                  fieldBoxBoundaryLo
outflow                 fieldBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                fieldBoxBoundaryHi

#PARTICLEBOXBOUNDARY
0                       iSpecies
inflow                  particleBoxBoundaryLo
outflow                 particleBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryLo
periodic                particleBoxBoundaryHi

#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

#HALLTERM
F                       useHallTerm

#RESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
0.0                     electronTemperature  [eV]
1.0                     electronGamma
1.0                     electronDensity0

#INFLOW
5.0                      rho [amu/cc]
20.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                      uy [km/s]
0.0                      uz [km/s]
10000.0                  T [K]

#BSUBCYCLE
1                       nBSubcycle

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
20.0                    ux [km/s]      uniform bulk flow along +x (U_code = 0.2)
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
1.0439e-8               bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s] tNorm = 1 s; sets cLight_SI = uNormSI

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
2000                    nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn
10.0                    dt
1                       dx

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
10.0                    TimeMax   ~1.6 ion gyroperiods (stability)

#RUN
